.env

# dist/ is tracked on purpose so main can be served directly. It is build
# output, so it is only correct as of the commit that carries it — regenerate
# with `npm run build` and commit it alongside any source change, or what is
# served stops matching what is in src/.
#
# The bundle carries VITE_SUPABASE_URL and the anon key, inlined by Vite at
# build time. (The CI workflow's comment claiming these are read at runtime is
# wrong: a build made without them produces an app that throws on boot.) That
# is what an anon key is for — it ships in client JavaScript in every
# deployment, and RLS is what actually guards the data. The service role key
# must never reach a build.

